WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:05.160
(Ana speaking Italian)
(Massimo speaking Italian)

00:00:05.468 --> 00:00:08.051
(gentle music)

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:18.150
- Welcome to the Academy.

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:19.678
- Thank you.

00:00:19.678 --> 00:00:24.011
And I'm honored to be in
front of this conversation.

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:27.390
- You are very welcome.

00:00:27.390 --> 00:00:30.360
The Academy deserves to
have people like you,

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:34.200
and I'm really proud to be
a member of the Academy.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.970
Also, because they're open.

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:40.290
They like to have more members worldwide.

00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:42.480
That helps everyone.

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:44.400
Because I mean, we see more movies.

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:48.450
- To be part of one of
many points of view,

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:50.160
I think it is an amazing thing.

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:54.357
When you see a movie, you see the movie,

00:00:57.505 --> 00:00:58.408
you can't know how much work is behind...

00:00:58.408 --> 00:01:00.241
For example, sometime,

00:01:02.741 --> 00:01:04.920
you don't know how much digital
stuff is into the movie,

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:06.216
how much makeup...

00:01:06.216 --> 00:01:08.141
- But we talk about that.

00:01:08.141 --> 00:01:08.974
We talk about that.

00:01:08.974 --> 00:01:11.974
(foreign language)

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:23.640
- Can you believe, Ana,

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:28.590
we were together in the
2005, doing "Volver."

00:01:28.590 --> 00:01:30.210
- We met there, in "Volver."

00:01:30.210 --> 00:01:33.360
- Big maestro, Pedro Almodovar.

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:34.980
We met in "Volver."

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:39.980
I met Penelope Cruz, and
I met Pedro Almodovar.

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:45.410
For me, it was a very intense experience,

00:01:45.618 --> 00:01:47.760
and a very beautiful experience.

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:49.680
- I remember when they say,

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:50.513
you say when

00:01:52.650 --> 00:01:54.630
their hair up like a acconciatura,

00:01:54.630 --> 00:01:57.819
so we were laughing about
the way that you say

00:01:57.819 --> 00:01:59.325
the words in Italian.

00:01:59.325 --> 00:02:00.158
- For the translation-

00:02:00.158 --> 00:02:01.140
- Now we say a acconciatura.

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:04.440
- Actually, for me to be in Spain,

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:07.530
17 years ago I didn't speak Spanish.

00:02:07.530 --> 00:02:11.370
I speak less English
actually than I speak now.

00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:13.800
The first time I remember that I arrived

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:18.800
with a shirt, clean shirt,
before to do the fitting.

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:20.790
After the fitting,

00:02:20.790 --> 00:02:25.650
I was completely sweat
from the excitement.

00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:30.120
I'm a fan of Pedro, I'm a fan of Penelope.

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:33.420
Then I become fan of you, for sure,

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:34.860
and friend more than fan.

00:02:34.860 --> 00:02:39.810
It was very intense moments
that we share in "Volver,"

00:02:39.810 --> 00:02:41.640
especially in the prep,

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:42.990
because Ped...

00:02:42.990 --> 00:02:46.470
do you remember the reference
that we speaking about,

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:48.330
actually was all Italian,

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:51.123
with all the reference,

00:02:52.417 --> 00:02:55.590
all preference from Anna Magnani-

00:02:55.590 --> 00:02:56.423
- Sophia-

00:02:57.465 --> 00:02:58.830
- And Sophia Loren.

00:02:58.830 --> 00:03:01.290
- You cannot be good if

00:03:01.290 --> 00:03:02.580
there is not a teamwork.

00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:04.440
It's really important for us,

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:07.050
I mean, to be like a really good team.

00:03:07.050 --> 00:03:08.262
We can do it well,

00:03:08.262 --> 00:03:09.570
but if the actor or the
actress doesn't do well,

00:03:09.570 --> 00:03:10.980
I mean we don't trust it.

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:13.620
We did really great jobs
when we did our job,

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:16.800
and the actor, like wow,
they look like them.

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:19.843
So with Penelope or with
Javier, they look like them.

00:03:19.843 --> 00:03:23.943
- I can just add that you say,

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:28.890
two people play with the harmony.

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:31.290
It's like two musicians.

00:03:31.290 --> 00:03:33.450
You have to have harmony in the music.

00:03:33.450 --> 00:03:35.089
- And bueno, one director.

00:03:35.089 --> 00:03:38.190
- Proud to do this job.

00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:41.400
Known to do hair, for my case,

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:44.820
It's not like to do my job

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:47.070
and be happy what the job I did,

00:03:47.070 --> 00:03:49.410
but to be part of this job.

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:51.780
It's a beautiful thing.

00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:54.210
- Use a line on me you've
never road-tested on anyone,

00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:55.043
I dare you.

00:03:59.064 --> 00:03:59.897
(soft music)

00:03:59.897 --> 00:04:01.510
- Will you like to learn how to rumba?

00:04:02.670 --> 00:04:03.503
- All right.

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:08.880
- I could never think
about to be here today.

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:11.790
- And I never thought that
I gonna be living in L.A.,

00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:13.230
I mean, and working in L.A.

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:15.210
It was a hard, really hard,

00:04:15.210 --> 00:04:17.370
but it really, I mean it was worth it.

00:04:17.370 --> 00:04:19.050
You start from zero there.

00:04:19.050 --> 00:04:23.010
Like I have been working
30 years in Europe,

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:24.570
but you arrive there and nobody knows you.

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:27.030
They make me like to work.

00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:28.290
I mean, I'm in the committee.

00:04:28.290 --> 00:04:31.470
Now I'm in judging short films.

00:04:31.470 --> 00:04:34.560
I mean, I'm really active
with that because I like it.

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:35.970
The difference that there is

00:04:35.970 --> 00:04:40.563
when you work with Europe,
Italy, I mean France, UK, I mean,

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:43.080
everyone works another way.

00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:45.300
I mean, between heads of departments,

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:47.040
I mean, it's the same or not.

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:50.130
It's just, you need to make that work.

00:04:50.130 --> 00:04:52.833
I think it's part of
our job, make that work.

00:04:52.833 --> 00:04:54.870
- The most of the people

00:04:54.870 --> 00:04:59.640
is easily adapt of any situation.

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:04.640
Our job meets any inconvenience
of weather, of location.

00:05:07.590 --> 00:05:09.750
You go to shoot in other country

00:05:09.750 --> 00:05:11.550
with a different culture,

00:05:11.550 --> 00:05:13.905
a very important element,

00:05:13.905 --> 00:05:16.410
that's because when
you go in other country

00:05:16.410 --> 00:05:17.520
with another culture,

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:19.680
you are a guest to work there,

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:22.005
and so you must keep-

00:05:22.005 --> 00:05:23.340
- Sometimes you're not welcome.

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:25.440
- Yeah, so you can do the circus,

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:27.460
but you have to do with the respect

00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:30.540
in the land where you doing that.

00:05:30.540 --> 00:05:34.430
- The last movie that I did in
L.A. was "Being the Ricardos"

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:36.150
in the middle of the pandemic,

00:05:36.150 --> 00:05:38.220
and the early '40s and '50s.

00:05:38.220 --> 00:05:39.717
It was kind of like,

00:05:39.717 --> 00:05:41.760
because it's really American,

00:05:41.760 --> 00:05:43.800
and then it was like red lips.

00:05:43.800 --> 00:05:46.020
I mean, it is like with all the masks

00:05:46.020 --> 00:05:48.465
and I was quite like,
"Okay, I gonna do it.

00:05:48.465 --> 00:05:50.760
I gonna do it, because it's
the period that I love it."

00:05:50.760 --> 00:05:53.370
And I really like it that they accept me,

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:54.720
but you need to work for that.

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:56.310
Of course not easy,

00:05:56.310 --> 00:05:58.920
but for a makeup or a hair stylist

00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:01.860
that wants to start in that business,

00:06:01.860 --> 00:06:05.624
States is the the best place to.

00:06:05.624 --> 00:06:08.700
I mean, you have more opportunities
than any other country.

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:13.260
- It's unbelievable how
all the member of the crew,

00:06:13.260 --> 00:06:17.760
actually, I know that we
have a different way to work

00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:22.760
in Europe than the States, than
maybe France, maybe England.

00:06:22.830 --> 00:06:25.330
I met people that remind me

00:06:26.337 --> 00:06:27.450
of people that I met already.

00:06:27.450 --> 00:06:32.250
In the end, this kind of
job is a very universal.

00:06:32.250 --> 00:06:35.100
- It's good to know the
way that people do things.

00:06:35.100 --> 00:06:37.890
Like a wig can be done for one hand

00:06:37.890 --> 00:06:38.920
in one way or another way.

00:06:38.920 --> 00:06:39.840
- Sure.
- I mean,

00:06:39.840 --> 00:06:43.890
I think it's good to work with more people

00:06:43.890 --> 00:06:47.160
and see different cultures,
different countries.

00:06:47.160 --> 00:06:47.993
I like it.

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:50.550
- You're in control, buddy.

00:06:52.620 --> 00:06:54.609
- You with the store or something?

00:06:54.609 --> 00:06:55.442
- No, I'm not with the store,

00:06:55.442 --> 00:06:56.400
but I'm gonna escort you out of it.

00:06:56.400 --> 00:06:58.171
- See what happens.
- Yeah.

00:06:58.171 --> 00:06:59.004
- What's gonna happen?

00:06:59.004 --> 00:06:59.837
Something bad's gonna happen?

00:06:59.837 --> 00:07:00.670
- Yeah.

00:07:01.853 --> 00:07:03.451
- Hah, outside.

00:07:03.451 --> 00:07:04.590
We're going outside.

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:08.120
- Sometimes people ask
me what I need to do

00:07:08.120 --> 00:07:10.803
to be there, to doing that,

00:07:12.882 --> 00:07:14.220
to do these kind of movies.

00:07:14.220 --> 00:07:15.420
You need to love,

00:07:15.420 --> 00:07:17.410
I mean you, you need to have the movies

00:07:18.334 --> 00:07:19.200
that really love what you are doing.

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:20.250
Things comes to you.

00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:22.260
I don't know, it's not that we are lucky.

00:07:22.260 --> 00:07:26.040
It's like we work hard
to do well our work,

00:07:26.040 --> 00:07:27.420
because we really trust,

00:07:27.420 --> 00:07:29.010
and sometimes you're doing something

00:07:29.010 --> 00:07:30.210
or you're gonna do something,

00:07:30.210 --> 00:07:31.043
and I cannot sleep.

00:07:31.043 --> 00:07:32.590
I mean, I'm in bed, thinking

00:07:33.681 --> 00:07:34.673
what I gonna do tomorrow?

00:07:35.720 --> 00:07:37.200
It's like nonstop.

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:38.880
But, I mean, I love it.

00:07:38.880 --> 00:07:41.313
- You say you must love, sure.

00:07:42.180 --> 00:07:44.400
But I want to say what I said before,

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:49.400
about to believe in the
beautyness of your dream.

00:07:49.530 --> 00:07:54.530
Doesn't mean to believe
in your dream directly,

00:07:54.690 --> 00:07:57.690
but just in the light of your dream.

00:07:57.690 --> 00:08:02.523
You must feel this job,
you must, to enjoy.

00:08:03.450 --> 00:08:06.270
If not, it's become like another job.

00:08:06.270 --> 00:08:11.270
You must feel the
happiness when the director

00:08:11.790 --> 00:08:16.790
or your people, your team
is happy what you are doing,

00:08:18.270 --> 00:08:20.010
or what all we doing.

00:08:20.010 --> 00:08:23.482
And you feel happy,
means it is a good scene,

00:08:23.482 --> 00:08:24.810
that you like this job.

00:08:24.810 --> 00:08:26.280
- Technique is everything.

00:08:26.280 --> 00:08:29.550
But even it's kind of nonstop,

00:08:29.550 --> 00:08:33.270
because you always are, new products,

00:08:33.270 --> 00:08:36.720
and it's good to know,
to see other people.

00:08:36.720 --> 00:08:38.100
Even if the result is the same,

00:08:38.100 --> 00:08:41.010
sometimes people do things in another way,

00:08:41.010 --> 00:08:42.870
and it's good they can.

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:45.102
The day that we stop learning

00:08:45.102 --> 00:08:46.500
is the day that I will stop working.

00:08:46.500 --> 00:08:51.060
- If, what I can say about
myself, younger myself,

00:08:51.060 --> 00:08:53.297
don't change nothing,

00:08:53.297 --> 00:08:54.390
(Ana laughing)

00:08:54.390 --> 00:08:56.070
don't move nothing.

00:08:56.070 --> 00:08:58.980
Do what you did without change.

00:08:58.980 --> 00:09:03.510
Because I think all the process need time,

00:09:03.510 --> 00:09:07.383
and this process take me where I am today,

00:09:08.220 --> 00:09:11.363
and all the experience
and movie that I did.

00:09:13.431 --> 00:09:15.830
(tense music)

00:09:15.830 --> 00:09:18.830
(foreign language)

00:09:30.630 --> 00:09:32.760
- When are we gonna work
together another time?

00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:33.593
I'm missing you.

00:09:33.593 --> 00:09:35.250
- Oh, hope soon.

00:09:35.250 --> 00:09:36.660
In the magic movie,

00:09:36.660 --> 00:09:41.660
any movie that we do, anyway,
is a experience of our lives.

00:09:41.790 --> 00:09:44.010
- Yes, wherever they take us.

00:09:44.010 --> 00:09:48.942
- Thank you Ana, because to
share with this conversation.

00:09:48.942 --> 00:09:50.766
- Always it's a pleasure.

00:09:50.766 --> 00:09:51.599
- Thank you.

00:09:51.599 --> 00:09:52.980
- Thank you.

00:09:52.980 --> 00:09:53.973
Love you, Massimo.

00:09:55.566 --> 00:09:58.149
(upbeat music)

